From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: David Heidelberg <david@ixit.cz>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 16:04:59 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 11/15] power: supply: qcom_smbx: Do not interfere with vbus
 driver

Charger should not touch bits handled by OTG block handled by the vbus
driver.

Signed-off-by: David Heidelberg <david@ixit.cz>

[nura-builds: adapted to the sdm845-7.1-rc1 tree, which has separate SMB2 and SMB5
init sequences: removed from the SMB2 one (PMI8998, PM660) only; the OTG_CFG definitions stay
for SMB5]
---
 drivers/power/supply/qcom_smbx.c | 2 --
 1 file changed, 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_smbx.c b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_smbx.c
index 9386adfb7..876f27ff2 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_smbx.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_smbx.c
@@ -823,8 +823,6 @@ static const struct smb_init_register smb2_init_seq[] = {
 	{ .addr = TYPE_C_CFG,
 	  .mask = FACTORY_MODE_DETECTION_EN_BIT | VCONN_OC_CFG_BIT,
 	  .val = 0 },
-	/* Configure VBUS for software control */
-	{ .addr = OTG_CFG, .mask = OTG_EN_SRC_CFG_BIT, .val = 0 },
 	/*
 	 * Use VBAT to determine the recharge threshold when battery is full
 	 * rather than the state of charge.
